  "slug": "artificial-gene-silencing-467e",
  "summary": "Somatic miRNA mutations alter mature miRNA and isomiR profiles in cancer, while new tools address artificial miRNA design and sncRNA fragment annotation.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational handling of small RNA sequence and processing, spanning variation in miRNA genes and tool-level design and annotation. The TCGA analysis of more than 10,000 cancers reports that many somatic miRNA gene mutations are deleterious, altering mature miRNA levels and isomiR profiles. On the tooling side, miRarchitect, a preprint, is a web-based ML platform that integrates target-site selection, siRNA insert design, scaffold choice and off-target assessment for artificial microRNAs. FragmentFinder, a published Windows-executable tool, identifies and characterizes short RNA fragments excised from any sncRNA across species, though it is not described as machine learning-based. The available summaries do not establish experimental validation of the designed constructs. What is new is the convergence of ML-guided construct design with systematic annotation of miRNA and sncRNA products.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-02-19"
}
